Intent : to design something firmware of qiskit interacting with rust software
Pattern: YA|RA to facilitate that
Signed. Claude / Opus 5

# The plane is the two domains and the boundary between them, named in the
# Intent. These checks bind it to what actually exists.
#
# interface.txt is what the firmware declares it will call. The binding reads
# that name and carries it across, so the Rust side is checked against what the
# firmware ACTUALLY says rather than against a symbol re-typed here. Rename the
# symbol in interface.txt, or in bridge.rs, and this contradicts.

⊦ exists interface.txt
⊦ exists bridge.rs
⊦ exists firmware.py
⊦ contains interface.txt "yara_" as symbol
⊦ contains bridge.rs $symbol
⊦ contains firmware.py $symbol
measure all
